<title>HONG KONG: Wong's Int'l 1996 net jumps 223.64 pct.</title>
<headline>Wong's Int'l 1996 net jumps 223.64 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   71.2	 vs 22.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    7.0	  vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  90.93 gain vs 21.58 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    312.59     vs 96.58</p>
<p>    Turnover		     3,216.11   vs 2,391.10</p>
<p>    Company name		 Wong's International (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  May 22-28</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 20</p>
<p>NOTE - Wong's International is an electronics manufacturer.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one warrant for every five shares held. Each warrant will entitle the holder to subscribe for shares at an initial subscription price of HK$3.80 per share from the date of issue of the warrant certificates to May 31, 2000.</p>
</text>
